{
  "schema_version": "govmem-aggregate-only-release-allowlist-v1",
  "release_name": "govmem-aggregate-only-v3",
  "description": [
    "Explicit allowlist for the conservative, AGGREGATE-ONLY public release of the",
    "GovMem v3 experiment. This is stricter than the earlier Tier-B allowlist: no",
    "row-level score file is shipped at all. The builder",
    "(scripts/build_public_release_candidate.py) copies ONLY the files matched by",
    "`include`, subtracts `exclude`, applies the documented `sanitize_rules` text",
    "substitutions, then runs the public-data audit (`forbidden_patterns`). If any",
    "copied file still contains a forbidden pattern the build fails closed and",
    "writes nothing.",
    "",
    "Anything not matched by `include` is excluded by construction. This is a",
    "deny-by-default selection: the candidate is never produced by copying the",
    "repository.",
    "",
    "Excluded by design (present in the developer tree, absent here): the row-level",
    "Tier-B score files (results/final_main_tier_b/**), every per-example cohort /",
    "judge-request / validation / observation / ledger / manifest JSONL, every",
    "per-instance and per-base CSV, and every content-fingerprint or source-derived",
    "identifier token. Only aggregate tables, aggregate summaries, protocol and",
    "readiness documentation, code, offline tests, and non-secret configs remain."
  ],
